---
import { getEntry, render } from "astro:content";
import Document from "../layouts/Document.astro";
import RfcHeader from "../components/RfcHeader.astro";
import { SCHEMA_PATH, SITE_URL, SOURCE_URL, VERSION, lastUpdated } from "../lib/site";

const entry = await getEntry("docs", "spec");
if (!entry) throw new Error("axp/SPEC.md not found");
const { Content, headings } = await render(entry);
const toc = headings.filter((h) => h.depth === 2).map(({ slug, text }) => ({ slug, text }));
---

<Document
  title="AXP: Agent Xchange Protocol"
  description="Coding agents run in isolation. AXP lets phones, browsers and other computers watch and steer running agent sessions, keeps every copy in sync, and makes remote commands safe to resend. Logs are ATXF transcripts."
  current="/"
  headings={toc}
>
  <RfcHeader
    slot="header"
    designator={`AXP/${VERSION}`}
    title="Agent Xchange Protocol"
    fields={[
      { label: "Status", kind: "status", value: "Draft" },
      { label: "Version", kind: "text", value: VERSION },
      { label: "Updated", kind: "date", value: lastUpdated("SPEC.md") },
      { label: "Author", kind: "text", value: "Leo Ostera" },
      { label: "Conventions", kind: "link", value: "MUST, SHOULD and MAY as in RFC 2119", href: "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2119" },
      { label: "Logs", kind: "link", value: "ATXF 0.1", href: "https://atxf.leostera.dev" },
      { label: "Schema", kind: "copy", value: `${SITE_URL}${SCHEMA_PATH}` },
      { label: "Source", kind: "link", value: "axp/SPEC.md", href: `${SOURCE_URL}SPEC.md` },
    ]}
  >
    <p>
      Coding agents run in isolation, each session on one machine and steerable only from the terminal it runs in. Sharing a finished transcript is solved by files such as <a href="https://atxf.leostera.dev">ATXF</a>. Working with a session that is still running, from a phone, a browser or another computer, is not: every tool invents its own way to send it commands, keep copies in sync, and know whether a prompt actually ran.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4">
      AXP solves them once, for any agent. A <strong>host</strong> runs Sessions and is the only writer of each one's log, a <strong>hub</strong> connects hosts and clients that cannot reach each other, and a <strong>client</strong> shows Sessions and sends commands. This document is the core; everything specific to an agent or a terminal is an <a href="/extensions/">extension</a>.
    </p>
  </RfcHeader>
  <Content />
</Document>
